fe/tools/mutation/fixtures/** -text

# The report skeleton's maintenance-contract fragments are byte-exact input to
# `split_body`: a CRLF-normalizing checkout would silently change where blocks
# split and break the byte round-trip (#1185 §2.5). The files land in S2; the
# declaration goes first so no checkout ever sees them untyped.
#
# `track_report*.md`, not `track_report_*.md`: the underscore-suffixed form misses
# a plain `track_report.md`, and a fragment file that silently falls outside this
# rule is exactly the failure it exists to prevent — nothing here breaks if the
# pattern is wider than the set of files that ever appears.
crates/calm-types/src/track_report*.md -text

# `report/legacy_initial_v4.md` is the frozen pre-header default body (#1635
# S2a): byte-exact input to the header-less compatibility fallback of
# `report_startup_read_required`. A CRLF checkout would silently change the
# frozen bytes and every pre-header track would read as "written".
crates/calm-types/src/report/*.md -text

# Agent-facing prompt sources are byte-exact input to `include_str!` (#1635):
# a CRLF checkout would change the rendered prompt and break its golden.
crates/calm-server/prompts/** -text
